<title>USA: Schick to acquire Keystone X-Ray.</title>
<headline>Schick to acquire Keystone X-Ray.</headline>
<dateline>LONG ISLAND CITY, N.Y. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schick Technologies Inc said Monday that it has signed a letter of intent to acquire for cash certain assets of Keystone X-Ray, Inc, a manufacturer of x-ray equipment for the medical and dental radiology field.</p>
<p>In a press release, Schick said it expects to close the transaction within 90 days.</p>
<p>A company spokesman was not immediately available to elaborate on terms of the transaction.</p>
<p>Keystone possesses a technology that enables it to produce a low-cost, high stability x-ray tube.</p>
</text>
